    "result_text": "The build passes. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What changed\n\n**customerCode format:** `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2192 `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`\n\n- `AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2014 now derives `CITY3` (upper-cased first 3 letters of `city`), keeps `LAST3` (first 3 of `lastName`), and computes `NNNN` as a **per-city** sequence: one more than the number of existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitive), instead of a global count. Short cities are handled the same way as short last names (`Math.min(3, ...)`). Example: `SYD-SMI-0007`.\n\n**Values derived from customerCode:**\n- `membershipNumber` (in `OwnerMapper.java`) is built as `<customerCode>-M<YY>` directly from `getCustomerCode()`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`). Updated its javadoc example.\n\n**Docs kept in sync:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 updated the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` descriptions/examples to the new format.\n\nThe stored column `customer_code VARCHAR(20)` comfortably fits the new 12-char format.\n\n## Tests\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserts `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) passes.\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
